The animate() function is called recursively using requestAnimationFrame() to update and redraw the particles on the canvas every frame. In the update() method of the Particle class, the particles' positions are updated based on their velocity, and collision detection logic is implemented to handle collisions between particles and the walls, as well as between particles themselves.

Overall, this code demonstrates a simple but effective algorithm for simulating particle collisions using JavaScript and the HTML Canvas.

