For the system of inequalities:

**(1)** $\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x＞1-x①\\ x+2＜4x-1②\end{array}\right.$

- Solving inequality ①:
  \begin{align*}
  2x + x &＞ 1 \\
  3x &＞ 1 \\
  x &＞ \frac{1}{3}
  \end{align*}

- Solving inequality ②:
  \begin{align*}
  x - 4x &＜ -1 - 2 \\
  -3x &＜ -3 \\
  x &＞ 1
  \end{align*}

Therefore, the solution set of the system of inequalities is $\boxed{x \gt 1}$.

**(2)** $\left\{\begin{array}{l}\frac{2}{3}x+5＞1-x①\\ x-1≤\frac{3}{4}x-\frac{1}{8}②\end{array}\right.$

- Solving inequality ①:
  \begin{align*}
  \frac{2}{3}x + x &＞ 1 - 5 \\
  \frac{5}{3}x &＞ -4 \\
  x &＞ -\frac{12}{5}
  \end{align*}

- Solving inequality ②:
  \begin{align*}
  x - \frac{3}{4}x &≤ -\frac{1}{8} + 1 \\
  \frac{1}{4}x &≤ \frac{7}{8} \\
  x &≤ \frac{7}{2}
  \end{align*}

Therefore, the solution set of the system of inequalities is $\boxed{-\frac{12}{5}＜x≤\frac{7}{2}}$.

