Let the work efficiency per minute of A be $x$, and that of B be $y$,

$$
\begin{align*}
30x + 25y &= 1 \\
24x + 30y &= 1
\end{align*}
$$

Solving these equations, we get

$$
\begin{align*}
x &= \frac{1}{60} \\
y &= \frac{1}{50}
\end{align*}
$$

Therefore, the time required for A and B to complete the document individually is $1 \div \frac{1}{60} = 60$ minutes for A, and $1 \div \frac{1}{50} = 50$ minutes for B.

Hence, the correct option is $\boxed{\text{B}}$.

